          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—cost-event evidence is missing\n\nI verified the target work order and the September Pending Close cutoff, but **cannot determine whether an event was created after that cutoff** from the available records.\n\n| Requested item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, Dekoven 1500 / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Cannot determine** |\n\nThe work order and cutoff come from the supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records in `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`. The timestamp is reproduced exactly as stored; no time-zone offset was supplied.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that, during **Pending Close**, newly created transactions falling in that period or an earlier period **will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to process, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing.**\n\n*Source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\nThus, a newly created, non-exempt transaction after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held while September remains Pending Close. Its lateness would be:\n\n`(event-created time − 2025-09-30T18:00:00) ÷ 60 seconds`\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe available input contains work-order and cost-period rows but **no cost-event rows**. The assigned supporting-records service repeatedly returned **“Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** This is missing evidence—not proof that no late event occurred. The event record is required to establish its transaction ID, amount, timestamp, accounting status, and policy consistency.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_0590951d1679/audit-report.json`.",
